Subject: gfx_sdl2: ask SDL for a high-DPI window on iOS

Without SDL_WINDOW_ALLOW_HIGHDPI, SDL's UIKit Metal view takes
contentScaleFactor 1.0, so the CAMetalLayer's drawable is the window's size in
POINTS and the whole game renders at a ninth of the pixels the panel has
(844x390 instead of 2532x1170 on the lane-3 iPhone 17e) and is upscaled by the
compositor. It looks like a soft texture filter and it is not one; it is the
single most common silent regression in this family of ports, and it survives
a screenshot because the screenshot is upscaled too.

Measured on the simulator before this patch: `state` reported
drawable=844x390, contents_scale=3.00, native_resolution=MISMATCH. After it,
drawable=2532x1170 and the assertion in scripts/sim-validate.sh passes - that
assertion exists precisely because this is invisible by eye.

The replay gate still runs at 844x390, through PD_IOS_RENDER_SCALE=1 in the
ANGLE glue, because the committed oracle frame is that size and a pixel diff
is only a gate at matched resolution.

diff --git a/port/fast3d/gfx_sdl2.cpp b/port/fast3d/gfx_sdl2.cpp
index 0eb8b0530..56df84d34 100644
--- a/port/fast3d/gfx_sdl2.cpp
+++ b/port/fast3d/gfx_sdl2.cpp
@@ -138,6 +138,13 @@ static void gfx_sdl_init(const struct GfxWindowInitSettings *set) {
     window_height = set->height;
 
 #ifdef SDL_HINT_VIDEO_HIGHDPI_DISABLED
+    // On iOS the flag below is not enough on its own: SDL_CreateWindow strips
+    // SDL_WINDOW_ALLOW_HIGHDPI whenever this hint is set (SDL_video.c:1742),
+    // and Video.AllowHiDpi defaults to 0. A phone has one panel and one right
+    // answer, so the setting does not get to turn native resolution off here;
+    // PD_IOS_RENDER_SCALE (app/gfx/gfx_angle_egl.mm) is the render-scale lever
+    // instead, and it is what the seeded replay uses to match the oracle.
+#ifndef PLATFORM_IOS
     if (!set->allow_hidpi) {
         // HiDPI control, if available
         SDL_SetHint(SDL_HINT_VIDEO_HIGHDPI_DISABLED, "1");
@@ -146,6 +153,7 @@ static void gfx_sdl_init(const struct GfxWindowInitSettings *set) {
         SDL_SetHint(SDL_HINT_WINDOWS_DPI_AWARENESS, "permonitor");
 #endif
     }
+#endif
 #endif
 
     if (SDL_Init(SDL_INIT_VIDEO) != 0) {
@@ -207,6 +215,15 @@ static void gfx_sdl_init(const struct GfxWindowInitSettings *set) {
     // ANGLE draws into the window's CAMetalLayer; SDL must not make a GL
     // context of its own, so SDL_WINDOW_OPENGL must NOT be set here.
     flags |= SDL_WINDOW_METAL;
+#ifdef PLATFORM_IOS
+    // Without this SDL's Metal view takes contentScaleFactor 1.0 and the whole
+    // game renders at a third of the panel's pixels and is upscaled by the
+    // compositor - a soft picture that looks like a filtering bug and is not
+    // one. With it the drawable is UIScreen.nativeScale x points, i.e. the
+    // 2532x1170 the iPhone 17e actually has. The charter's acceptance is
+    // "native drawable resolution"; this is the line that makes it true.
+    flags |= SDL_WINDOW_ALLOW_HIGHDPI;
+#endif
 #else
     flags |= SDL_WINDOW_OPENGL;
 #endif
